  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lima Joint Advocacy Urban Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project forms the advocacy and organisational strengthening component of programme PER-13-01, a joint project with partners EDUCA, IES, Solidaridad and Warmi Huasi. 

The project aims to facilitate the participation of marginalised urban communities in a situation of vulnerability, especially young people, children and women in decision-making processes to guarantee their rights, their access to assets, services and sustainable livelihoods. The partners will carry out diagnoses of needs with their own target groups and together will define an advocacy plan to achieve the change they want to attain. The advocacy plan will be implemented over the course of the three-year cycle and the participating groups accompanied and strengthened, in order to achieve the desired change.</narrative>
  </description>
